            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03392-6</link>
            <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature, Published online: 26 October 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03392-6"&gt;doi:10.1038/d41586-026-03392-6&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;An eloquent analysis of the origins of human speech suggests that social cohesion, not conflict, drove our use of words.</content:encoded>
            <dc:title>Women might have invented language — but not alone</dc:title>
            <dc:creator>Andrew Robinson</dc:creator>
            <dc:identifier>doi:10.1038/d41586-026-03392-6</dc:identifier>
            <dc:date>2026-10-26</dc:date>
