        <source url="https://www.nature.com/nature.rss">https://www.nature.com/nature.rss</source><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03392-6</guid><ns3:identity>doi:10.1038/d41586-026-03392-6</ns3:identity><ns3:identity>guid:https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03392-6</ns3:identity><ns3:identity>url:https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03392-6</ns3:identity></item><item><title>Are salaries getting worse? Many scientists think so</title>
            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03398-0</link>
            <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature, Published online: 26 October 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03398-0"&gt;doi:10.1038/d41586-026-03398-0&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;Nature’s survey of almost 4,000 researchers shows that you’re not alone if you struggle to make ends meet or your last pay rise is a distant memory.</content:encoded>
            <dc:title>Are salaries getting worse? Many scientists think so</dc:title>
            <dc:creator>Linda Nordling</dc:creator>
            <dc:identifier>doi:10.1038/d41586-026-03398-0</dc:identifier>
            <dc:date>2026-10-26</dc:date>
            <ns2:publicationName>Nature</ns2:publicationName>
            <ns2:doi>10.1038/d41586-026-03398-0</ns2:doi>
            <ns2:url>https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03398-0</ns2:url>
        <source url="https://www.nature.com/nature.rss">https://www.nature.com/nature.rss</source><guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03398-0</guid><ns3:identity>doi:10.1038/d41586-026-03398-0</ns3:identity><ns3:identity>guid:https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03398-0</ns3:identity><ns3:identity>url:https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03398-0</ns3:identity></item><item><title>&lt;i&gt;The Selfish Gene&lt;/i&gt;, 50 years on — it’s time for an update</title>
            <link>https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03393-5</link>
            <content:encoded>
                &lt;p&gt;Nature, Published online: 26 October 2026; &lt;a href="https://www.nature.com/articles/d41586-026-03393-5"&gt;doi:10.1038/d41586-026-03393-5&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;A focus on the gene alone has become outdated. Books that capture the complexity of life deserve centre stage.</content:encoded>
            <dc:title>&lt;i&gt;The Selfish Gene&lt;/i&gt;, 50 years on — it’s time for an update</dc:title>
            <dc:creator>Nathaniel Comfort</dc:creator>
